{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/pricing.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:09:26.298330Z","id":"45b5c32244ff7d7410dfa5ab1f302154e8525e88903741fcbfd4943564dcde35","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs begin_step calls check_model_priced(tx, ov, model) without the key source, so a turn on an own key under require_explicit_price is refused before the run loop runs it. The store change that passes the key the person uses now (commit 2dcaf4b5f, 'fix(store): ... never refuse own-key runs for a price') makes the test pass: verified by applying it uncommitted and running bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all (both targets passed).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":284},"end":{"line":301},"content_hash":"b523150a98bcfecf195f7596843751ae3fc8b2bdccfd400975055e781f919cee"},"suggested_fix":"Remove the #[ignore] once check_model_priced takes the key source on this branch.","summary":"an_own_key_runs_an_unpriced_model_under_require_explicit_price is #[ignore]d: Store::begin_step refuses model_not_priced for any key on this branch","tags":["pricing","tests","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/pricing.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:14:01.818366Z","id":"ba290d7fa087224088bac83fabcd81dc54e5eb6efdc3f166b98602faddf29171","body":{"detail":"The only test reaching token_rate's own-key zero rate (run.rs:907-925) is an_own_key_runs_an_unpriced_model_under_require_explicit_price, which is #[ignore]d (45b5c322): deleting the fallback passes the suite. an_own_key_is_not_bounded_by_token_rates_it_is_not_charged covers only default rates (applies instance_key); affordable's other branch, an own key with a token rate that applies always, still bounding max_tokens, is untested.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":197},"end":{"line":213},"content_hash":"7407449eabf3a8855f5caf052aae324b05e9d56914fd6f4284963b3eb8583084"},"suggested_fix":"Unit-test token_rate (or Tick::rates) with require_explicit_price and no line on an own key; add a case where a token line applies always on an own key and max_tokens is bounded.","summary":"No running test exercises token_rate's own-key fallback or an own key bounded by a non-waived token rate","tags":["pricing","tests","review","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/pricing.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:25:36.293612Z","id":"b2ed8b67bfee6f1b74347ebffa2b1773f1863265e620ef241b4f2595e9c45393","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"45b5c32244ff7d7410dfa5ab1f302154e8525e88903741fcbfd4943564dcde35","summary":"Fixed in git:a9ecb07d1: the #[ignore] is removed and the test passes now that turns begin through Store::begin_step_on with the chosen key; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/pricing.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:25:36.295435Z","id":"c5eb9ba67671e74519e2b3e04d197b87e8d4021de6e1126c197cee9269d905e1","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ba290d7fa087224088bac83fabcd81dc54e5eb6efdc3f166b98602faddf29171","summary":"Fixed in git:a9ecb07d1: run::tests::an_own_key_is_charged_nothing_for_a_model_without_a_rate unit-tests token_rate's own-key fallback; pricing::an_own_key_is_bounded_by_a_token_line_that_always_applies (max_tokens 21 428 under 30 credits) and the un-ignored own-key run pass; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/pricing.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.605863Z","id":"09333c9f64d98e215ff9022c2fea91be8ea8b7b46c6429e20355c3cd1e1e4f14","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7abc1ef162f1","summary":"Fixed in git:7abc1ef16. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed in git:7abc1ef16: run::tests::an_own_key_is_charged_nothing_for_a_model_without_a_rate unit-tests token_rate's own-key fallback; pricing::an_own_key_is_bounded_by_a_token_line_that_always_applies (max_tokens 21 428 under 30 credits) and the un-ignored own-key run pass; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","supersedes":"ba290d7fa087224088bac83fabcd81dc54e5eb6efdc3f166b98602faddf29171","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/pricing.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.706556Z","id":"754410063f4307a3f31df87853d9ba6f4c8645b2b884038d37f9a125cd6a94e0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7abc1ef162f1","summary":"Fixed in git:7abc1ef16. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed in git:7abc1ef16: the #[ignore] is removed and the test passes now that turns begin through Store::begin_step_on with the chosen key; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","supersedes":"45b5c32244ff7d7410dfa5ab1f302154e8525e88903741fcbfd4943564dcde35","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:01:14.442016Z","id":"5105e631244ae859c3a507e51336cb006bf5197e2a132e990630ef5c2c52701e","body":{"detail":"Every ending test but finish_posts_its_summary_on_every_thread_of_a_run_that_did_not_reply (line 514) runs on one thread (Env::run), so four changes to crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs at f12121994 pass `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test` (both PASSED each time), each tried alone and reverted: (1) give_up (run.rs:1721-1740) posts its notice only when the run has fewer than two threads; (2) stop (run.rs:1549-1590) does the same; (3) finish (run.rs:1681-1719) also posts the summary on each thread the run did not reply on, when it replied on another (a per-thread rule in place of today's run-wide `hist.replied.is_empty()`, run.rs:1683); (4) finish posts when the summary is empty (`let post = self.hist.replied.is_empty();`). Limiting notify_at (run.rs:1514) to the first thread does fail ending.finish.no-reply.two-threads.json, at line 17. Notices and the finish rule are what docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md (\"What stays the same on clax.dev\": what ClaxBot replies and when) says must not change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":508},"end":{"line":582},"content_hash":"50ee74a9bcf8b0402778d7b62958038e1f106497214234056fbe1dda662feb9c"},"suggested_fix":"Add ending goldens on run_on_both_threads (line 321): a give_up, a stopped (a cap) and a failed run; a finish after a script that edited and replied on T1 alone (no summary on either thread today), the same with a fetched page (sources on both threads at NOTICE_SEQ+1 and +2); and a finish with an empty summary.","summary":"No ending golden has a two-thread run that gives up, stops, fails or replied on one thread: which threads get a notice is pinned for one case only (finish, no reply)","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:01:14.442093Z","id":"900d752fb269e3301c99d01185f6733ad9f2059dc3ba68974817b82bd5037ec5","body":{"detail":"Removing `self.deps.host.working(&self.run, false).await;` from give_up (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:1738) at f12121994 leaves `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test` PASSED (reverted after). FakeBotHost records every call (FakeState::working, crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs:761-763) and the only assertion on it is the first and last value of one finished run (crates/clax-bot/tests/runs.rs:73-74). On the server working(false) clears ClaxBot from the artifact's roster and starts the follow-ups that waited (crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs:1041-1063), so a missed call leaves a thread showing ClaxBot at work and its follow-up unstarted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":241},"end":{"line":266},"content_hash":"9edc86835aec32f352cfb359cc45ca0a037eece0c9244ef1cb5f2c2b74ec303d"},"suggested_fix":"Add the sequence of working calls to Pins::ending (\"roster\": [true, …, false]), so each ending golden pins it.","summary":"No golden pins the roster calls (BotHost::working): a run that gives up and never calls working(false) passes every clax-bot test","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:01:14.442139Z","id":"d3faaaaf88879a92b6d479e28dcdc7fe818ed201413880cef314693d24c9c7d0","body":{"detail":"`body[\"credits_milli\"] = json!(…)` (line 222) is serde_json's IndexMut, which adds the key when it is absent. With the fill of bot.script's credits_milli and the `.with(\"credits_milli\", total)` of bot.run_end both removed from crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs:1032-1042, `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test` still PASSED (reverted after); the file's header (lines 36-37) says a normalised value's key stays pinned. Because the replacement is chosen by kind, renaming the kind (\"bot.script\" to \"bot.scripted\" in crates/clax-core/src/audit/mod.rs:117) fails audit.thread.json with `First difference: line 83  golden: \"credits_milli\": \"<charged from what the scripts measured>\"  now: \"credits_milli\": 1`, which reads as a timing difference and not as a kind that changed. The replacement is also wider than its reason: audit.failed.json's run ran no script, and its bot.run_end credits are exact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":211},"end":{"line":235},"content_hash":"996db60aa02ab20df11b3571bf63ec1e0999613fbc904f40e7dfaf84236fb854"},"suggested_fix":"Replace the value only when the key is present and not null (as scrub does, lines 101-103), and put the kind in the message or compare kinds first (an assert_eq on the list of kinds before the golden).","summary":"Pins::audit inserts `credits_milli` into a bot.script or bot.run_end body that lacks it, so the key is not pinned; and a changed kind is reported as a changed credits_milli","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:01:14.442209Z","id":"5389bfc0a062a41d09a28b77133226c51c9582ddc28524379602880b077b976e","body":{"detail":"By reading, not by a mutation: next_after (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:791-796) answers all three tools with `The input of {name} does not match its schema; nothing ran.`, and answer.tool-input.not-its-schema.json holds the run_script case alone (line 926). A `finish` whose summary is not a string is the case a typed finish result changes first; today it is answered and the run goes on.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":904},"end":{"line":965},"content_hash":"8c3017dbfe6b14d830b5cc0daf3158db90a88fa44ed2182524673103555e3326"},"suggested_fix":"Add answer goldens for finish with {\"summary\": 1} and give_up with {}.","summary":"The answers to a `finish` or `give_up` call whose input does not match its schema are not pinned; only run_script's is","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:01:14.442245Z","id":"42b60e4a5a4261929defc82b3d5ff68758e27c44e7d6fd1f9bdac5fdc76332b2","body":{"detail":"Pinned from script/web.rs: limit and offset out of range (lines 368, 385), a private host (812), a URL not in prior context (845). Not pinned by any golden: the run's cap (`this run has used its {max} {what}; work with what you have`, 328-331), the query length (362), the three `turned off … since this run started` messages (352-355, 540-559; crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs:602 holds one by equality), `is not available to this run` (524-527), `Continue without the web.` (562-565), `this run already read … as …` (665-670; tests/web.rs:1141 by `contains`), pricing not configured (752-758; tests/web.rs:1111 by `contains`), credits left (768-775), the request that could not be read (821-825) and a credentialed URL (833-837). steps.thread.json has no web call, so a call's `cost_milli` and `web` fields (read by step_view, crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs:1409-1416) and a web call's journal result are unpinned. The conversion of a fetched page to text is in crates/clax-bot/src/web/markdown.rs with its own unit tests and is not what this note is about.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1190},"end":{"line":1233},"content_hash":"dbeca6270da73739dbe634a4253d911bb89d58197b59aab536a19e29b9603911"},"suggested_fix":"Extend the web script with the cap (a grant of one search), a query of 0 characters, a credentialed URL and a second fetch as raw; and pin steps, journal and audit of the fetched_then run (line 554) as the thread run's are.","summary":"Of the refusals crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs words for a model, script.web-operations.json pins four; and no golden holds the stored step, journal or audit records of a script that used the web","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:01:14.442282Z","id":"1f33eed79ce6775bd51820b8dd0ad7009faf10a8190193b5bdd0f6da7af114fe","body":{"detail":"request.thread.{1-first,2-after-a-script}.json, request.brief.{1-first,2-after-a-script}.json, the six request.*.wire.json and steps.{thread,brief}.json each hold the 12 KB system prompt; after_the_first (lines 294-301) already replaces it in requests 3 and 4 once the test has compared it with the first request's. A review of such a change cannot tell the 14 diffs apart from one another, and the habit of rewriting them unread is what makes a pin worthless. request.thread.2.wire.json and request.thread.3.wire.json add little: request 4's bytes hold every earlier message, and where the cache breakpoint sits in requests 2 and 3 is in their readable goldens.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":376},"end":{"line":435},"content_hash":"fea405d0914182c17c26905d4a4e8fb8ed6e6e21442225bf5f3fae732a7dcc32"},"suggested_fix":"Use after_the_first for the second requests, replace `system` in steps.*.json by a note after asserting it equals the first request's system text, and keep the wire golden of the first and the last request of each run.","summary":"The system prompt and the tools are held whole in 14 of the 60 fixtures, so one meant change of wording rewrites 14 files of 15 KB beside the 8 prompt goldens","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:01:14.442314Z","id":"48d144428bbcb897f6a4589b05357acf4117a9f5ee27cd21563f0f2d50af87c4","body":{"detail":"By reading: the only uses of `effort` under crates/clax-bot are its declaration, its default None and `effort: self.settings.effort.clone()` (src/run.rs:107, 138, 1902); `grep -n effort crates/clax-bot/tests/*.rs` finds nothing. Every golden run uses RunSettings::default() (crates/clax-bot/tests/common/mod.rs:527-530), so the request bodies hold no effort field.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":349},"end":{"line":375},"content_hash":"70749953a62d39f0e4eb65515dbadd45951f390d6f0bc63d154bdec3411226a2"},"suggested_fix":"Set an effort in the brief run (env.set) so request.brief.*.json and its wire goldens hold the field.","summary":"No pinned request sets RunSettings::effort, so a turn that stops sending it passes","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:01:26.504151Z","id":"31bfe4c2991e64a0d33f05cc3cafde16bf47367ca2420d0de2c138472f5e94b0","body":{"detail":"request.thread.{1-first,2-after-a-script}.json, request.brief.{1-first,2-after-a-script}.json, the six request.*.wire.json and steps.{thread,brief}.json each hold the 12 KB system prompt; after_the_first (lines 294-301) already replaces it in requests 3 and 4 once the test has compared it with the first request's. A review of such a change cannot tell the 12 diffs apart from one another, and the habit of rewriting them unread is what makes a pin worthless. request.thread.2.wire.json and request.thread.3.wire.json add little: request 4's bytes hold every earlier message, and where the cache breakpoint sits in requests 2 and 3 is in their readable goldens.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":376},"end":{"line":435},"content_hash":"fea405d0914182c17c26905d4a4e8fb8ed6e6e21442225bf5f3fae732a7dcc32"},"suggested_fix":"Use after_the_first for the second requests, replace `system` in steps.*.json by a note after asserting it equals the first request's system text, and keep the wire golden of the first and the last request of each run.","summary":"The system prompt and the tools are held whole in 12 of the 60 fixtures, so one meant change of wording rewrites 12 files of 15 KB beside the 8 prompt goldens","supersedes":"1f33eed79ce6775bd51820b8dd0ad7009faf10a8190193b5bdd0f6da7af114fe","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:25:14.434801Z","id":"fbe7b6d046b09fbc49d9e26765382acddec15ebe8fcef5725d2b66fbd9172441","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbbf78a0e","summary":"Fixed: six ending goldens on a run of two threads (crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/ending.give-up.two-threads.json, ending.stopped.run-cap.two-threads.json, ending.failed.two-threads.json, ending.finish.replied-on-one-of-two-threads.json, ending.finish.replied-on-one-of-two-threads.sources.json, ending.finish.empty-summary.two-threads.json). Evidence: each of the four changes to crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs the record names, made alone and reverted, now fails `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration` (exit 3, 158 passed; 1 failed): give_up posting only on a run of fewer than two threads fails a_run_on_two_threads_that_gives_up_says_so_on_both on ending.give-up.two-threads.json line 10; the same in stop fails a_cap_stops_a_run_on_two_threads_saying_so_on_both on ending.stopped.run-cap.two-threads.json line 9; finish posting the summary on each thread not replied on fails finish_posts_no_summary_on_any_thread_when_the_run_replied_on_one on ending.finish.replied-on-one-of-two-threads.json line 10; `let post = self.hist.replied.is_empty();` fails finish_posts_no_empty_summary on ending.finish.empty-summary.two-threads.json line 5 (golden `\"posted\": false`, now true).","supersedes":"5105e631244ae859c3a507e51336cb006bf5197e2a132e990630ef5c2c52701e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:25:14.850145Z","id":"5786ac81fb45ade87d330a835c2028f2f8f234de1153c95e47e8c7b7179ebdf0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4c7fb56e5","summary":"Fixed: Pins::ending holds `roster`, every BotHost::working call of the run in order, so each of the 33 ending.*.json goldens pins it. Evidence: with `self.deps.host.working(&self.run, false).await;` removed from give_up in crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs (reverted after), `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration` exits 3 with 153 passed; 6 failed: the give-up goldens ending.give-up.{context-window,refusal,model,no-tool-call,after-one-script-without-edits,two-threads}.json each differ at the roster's last line (golden `true,`, now `true`: the closing false is gone).","supersedes":"900d752fb269e3301c99d01185f6733ad9f2059dc3ba68974817b82bd5037ec5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:25:15.258653Z","id":"5a92e136f721541f9607bacbfed004ea4e7a2470822f9dfa5f58c1f52a1b06c1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4c7fb56e5","summary":"Fixed: Pins::audit replaces credits_milli only where the key is present with a value and is charged from a script's measurements (bot.script, and bot.run_end of a run that ran a script), and an audit golden starts with the list of its records' kinds. Evidence, each change made alone and reverted, `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration` exit 3: with the bot.script fill and bot.run_end's `.with(\"credits_milli\", total)` removed from crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs, 4 tests fail: audit.thread.json line 100, audit.brief.json line 90 and audit.web.json line 294 (golden `\"credits_milli\": \"<charged from what the scripts measured>\"`, now `\"error\": null`) and audit.failed.json line 46 (golden `\"credits_milli\": 0`, now `\"outcome\": \"failed\"`); with the kind renamed bot.scripted in crates/clax-core/src/audit/mod.rs, the first difference of audit.thread.json and audit.brief.json is line 5 and of audit.web.json line 11, golden `\"bot.script\"`, now `\"bot.scripted\"`, in the list of kinds.","supersedes":"d3faaaaf88879a92b6d479e28dcdc7fe818ed201413880cef314693d24c9c7d0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:25:15.998575Z","id":"8e90695eb424195608909fac6bea262b28bd29581b395b195d981b6af7b99a23","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbbf78a0e","summary":"Fixed: crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/answer.tool-input.finish-not-its-schema.json (finish with {\"summary\": 1}) and answer.tool-input.give-up-not-its-schema.json (give_up with {}). Evidence: with next_after in crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs answering finish alone `The result of finish is invalid; nothing ran.` (reverted after), `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration` exits 3 with 158 passed; 1 failed: finish_input_that_does_not_match_its_schema_is_answered_with_an_error, answer.tool-input.finish-not-its-schema.json line 21.","supersedes":"5389bfc0a062a41d09a28b77133226c51c9582ddc28524379602880b077b976e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:25:16.301729Z","id":"13cba825d78c61083d2df229721c6d22123cf5c7977ffa41693514d3569eb49c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbbf78a0e","summary":"Fixed: every refusal the record lists is pinned, in crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/script.web-operations.json (the query's length, a credentialed URL, a page already read in another format, the retryable suffix, and the refusals of crates/clax-bot/src/web/url.rs) or in script.web-refusals.json, whose cases are each a run of their own (the caps, an operation not declared, the three turned-off wordings, a source unusable here, pricing not configured, credits left, a request that cannot be read, own hosts and the admin's list on the URL and on a redirect); and steps.web.json, journal.web.json and audit.web.json hold a web run's step calls (cost_milli, web), journal results and bot.web records. Evidence: with the cap's words changed to `work with what you got` in crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs (reverted after), `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration` exits 3 with 158 passed; 1 failed: web_refusals_are_pinned, script.web-refusals.json line 71.","supersedes":"42b60e4a5a4261929defc82b3d5ff68758e27c44e7d6fd1f9bdac5fdc76332b2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:25:16.641167Z","id":"b26ce7c7a2e5b26fbe4f62d04bdbbe7e12182137d6aa7d2564581f8a55d91f04","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4c7fb56e5","summary":"Fixed as suggested: the second requests go through after_the_first, Pins::steps replaces the system text a run's first turn stores by a note after comparing it with the first request's, and the wire goldens are of a run's first and last request (request.thread.2.wire.json and request.thread.3.wire.json are removed). Evidence: `grep -c 'You are ClaxBot' crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/*` counts the prompt in 6 files (request.{thread,brief}.1-first.json, request.thread.{1,4}.wire.json, request.brief.{1,2}.wire.json), down from 12; the old and new readable goldens are equal once the old ones' system and tools are replaced by the note; `bazel test --runs_per_test=3 //crates/clax-bot:all` passes.","supersedes":"31bfe4c2991e64a0d33f05cc3cafde16bf47367ca2420d0de2c138472f5e94b0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:25:17.071150Z","id":"700f0a61fd61d669dd8e26bcabb97993d78e6153dda130fa54b9fca9caae03b3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4c7fb56e5","summary":"Fixed as suggested: a_brief_run_is_pinned sets RunSettings::effort to high, and request.brief.*.json and their wire goldens hold `output_config`. Evidence: with `effort: None` in place of `effort: self.settings.effort.clone()` in crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs (reverted after) at 44cdb9d0c, `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration` exits 3 with 158 passed; 1 failed: a_brief_run_is_pinned, on request.brief.1-first.json line 18 and request.brief.2-after-a-script.json line 46 (golden `\"output_config\": {`, now `\"stream\": true,`) and both brief wire goldens.","supersedes":"48d144428bbcb897f6a4589b05357acf4117a9f5ee27cd21563f0f2d50af87c4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:25:17.950171Z","id":"49ba727017e44f0127dceda958e0fe4c7a2aacdee079797bd2f3f7c30d7b28df","body":{"detail":"The goldens script.web-operations.json and script.web-refusals.json hold every message script/web.rs and src/web/url.rs word themselves. Not pinned, by reading: (1) the errors web.rs passes on from the store through host_error (WebAccess::now, bot_web_counts, bot_web_calls, web_pages, rate_of, one_request, week_usage, flags_of, the journal entry and spend_journaled; web.rs lines 504, 559, 573, 650, 750-794, 830): the tests' store is the real one and has no way to fail one read in the middle of a script; (2) `the host is a private or local address` (url.rs:100), which no http or https URL reaches, since url::Url refuses one without a host first; (3) the words a source answers itself: FakeWebSource's (src/web/fake.rs: a redirect from https to http, a redirect chain past the limit, a redirect to no URL) are the fake's, and the daemon's and the Worker's sources word their own outside this crate; (4) `clax.<op> is not available to this run` is driven by a run that did not declare the operation, not by a host without a source (Deps::web None), which answers the same words.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1698},"end":{"line":1707},"content_hash":"a0eee8cc0383fca38118b2af92b03f4204b3bbca4954c6dcd97458d0b191f531"},"suggested_fix":"If script/web.rs moves behind a session that can fail a read, pin one store error's passage then; pin the real sources' redirect and timeout words in the crates that hold them.","summary":"What a script can be told by crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs that no golden pins: a store error passed through as it is, and a fake source's own words","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:44:30.868687Z","id":"d17b70dfda2e90eac8b4916617bf9b217d8e859689ebf48f485a9ae0d4de71c3","body":{"detail":"Pins::ending lists the replies grouped by thread (Env::replies reads thread 1, then thread 2) and the notices' journal places without their thread. In crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:1515, `self.run.thread_ids.iter().rev().enumerate()` (thread 2 posted first, at NOTICE_SEQ) and `.iter().enumerate().rev()` (thread 2 posted first, at NOTICE_SEQ + 1) both pass, the six two-thread ending goldens included (ending.give-up.two-threads.json, ending.stopped.run-cap.two-threads.json, ending.failed.two-threads.json and the three finish ones). Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED. The close fbe7b6d046b09fbc49d9e26765382acddec15ebe8fcef5725d2b66fbd9172441 covers which threads get a notice, not this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":307},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"a0253b0a8968dfa5c591f85ed5ad28b9b3a5bde8764a5c07e00e00438a0f758f"},"suggested_fix":"Add to Pins::ending the fake host's committed reply writes in order (FakeState::writes, crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs:322-326: key, thread), or map each notice's journal entry to its thread.","summary":"An ending golden does not say which thread a notice went to or in what order they were posted: reversing the threads in notify_at passes the suite","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:44:30.868777Z","id":"9655610a5a1a53b96284b5dba4d2c8b8de4d88ba354f95ae9e24c5a6c39b2d57","body":{"detail":"Moving `self.deps.host.working(&self.run, false).await` to before `self.commit` in give_up (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:1727-1738) or in finish (run.rs:1707-1717) passes the suite. Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED. The order is behaviour: the server's working(false) starts the follow-ups only for a run that is terminal (crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs:1041-1067, crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs:983-992). With the finish change, `bazel test --test_arg=follow_up //crates/clax-server:integration__6` fails api_claxbot_run::comments_on_a_claxbot_thread_follow_up_on_their_authors_credits_and_rights (tests/api_claxbot_run.rs:565, `the condition held: Elapsed(())`, after 120 s; it passes in 1.4 s unchanged), so the order is held there alone, and slowly. The count of `true` is one per tick that reaches a turn or a script, attempts that fail to commit included (ending.failed.*.json hold three): each renews the 120 s working record (crates/clax-core/src/working.rs:12, 434).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":322},"end":{"line":332},"content_hash":"ce06136d213a04e10ef0c2d29f7f0155eb271c82d9055e4cdc1a554f1b2a7073"},"suggested_fix":"Have the fake host record with each working call whether the run was terminal in the store (or the run's status), and pin that in the roster.","summary":"The roster is a flat list of working calls, so no golden tells working(false) after the terminal commit from working(false) before it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:44:30.868847Z","id":"8edda3bc9d9bedabe3da147ab03e2f18f3a8765149d4b8c53dad1d93372c228e","body":{"detail":"journal.thread.json, journal.web.json and steps.{thread,brief,web}.json hold only files.read, files.replace, draft.check, draft.publish, threads.reply and the web operations. the_draft_operations_answers_are_pinned, a_publish_conflict_and_the_rebase_after_it_are_pinned and a_second_artifact_is_refused pin the tool result alone (script_result), whose calls carry op, ok and code. Passing changes, in crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs: files.write not journaled (line 392: `replay.is_none() && op != \"files.write\"`); draft.rebase journaled without its value (line 393, `false`), which a rebase made again reads its version from (lines 240-253); a refused publish not journaled (lines 399-401 removed); a rules refusal not journaled (lines 373-375 removed); and in crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs:739-753 the target of draft.rebase, or of files.write, made None. Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1230},"end":{"line":1266},"content_hash":"0e75d5849bd4a9deec48ebb7c258ee82cd113bbd8e6e1a84bd3d555ce3580922"},"suggested_fix":"Pin Pins::journal and the script step's `calls` for the draft-operations run and the rebase run (journal.draft-operations.json, journal.draft-rebase.json, or one golden each with result, calls and journal).","summary":"The journal rows and step `calls` of the draft-operations and rebase scripts are not pinned: six changes to what is journaled or to a call's target pass the suite","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:44:30.868901Z","id":"a71508ec56fc31b9b61354023cf879bcf316f7c2da8f2a2b4c0c4cae1669744b","body":{"detail":"(1) In finish (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:1687-1689), posting `{summary}{list}` on the first thread only passes the suite: finish.no-reply.sources and finish.no-reply.three-sources are runs of one thread, and finish.no-reply.two-threads fetched nothing. (2) In History::of (run.rs:629-630), `wrote` without `|| !p[\"published\"].is_null()` passes the suite: no run replies, then publishes from a script that changes no file (edits in one script, the reply in the next, the publish in a third). The `changed` half is held: without it ending.finish.replied-before-a-draft-write.json fails at `\"posted\"`. Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":680},"end":{"line":716},"content_hash":"663c95dbc513306824dcc5140c1370441c5e3347069891864fed1a2b64696786"},"suggested_fix":"fetched_then(\"\", true) pinned as finish.no-reply.two-threads.sources; and a run of three scripts (edit; reply; publish) pinned as finish.replied-before-a-publish.","summary":"Two halves of the finish rule have no golden: a summary with sources on a run of two threads that did not reply, and a reply made before a script that published without editing","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:44:30.868949Z","id":"1d7d88c87843a707187cb5b5e376f18c546ed98b5287e85206e0669d30c044f2","body":{"detail":"`push` (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:568-576) merges a message into the last one of the same role; the one case in a run is the assistant turn after a pause_turn. pin_answer pins the second request, which holds the paused turn alone; the merged message would be in a third. With the merged blocks put first (`m.content.splice(0..0, content)` at run.rs:573) the suite passes. Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED. With no merging at all only the unit test run::tests::history_merges_consecutive_turns_of_one_role fails, no golden.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1063},"end":{"line":1071},"content_hash":"bb897c673036e0ed8e11237fe81d45739c63b32e4d76b6f15572f1c9293cf66c"},"suggested_fix":"A run of a paused turn, a turn with no tool call and a finish, pinning the third request's messages.","summary":"No pinned request holds two turns of one role merged: answer.pause-turn.json is the request after the paused turn, before the turn that continues it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:44:30.868996Z","id":"7c5dd6f497da45c2a97d3d2c1cda745016e45385947cf31af584e176626a4f11","body":{"detail":"a_replay_that_diverged_is_pinned is the only golden of a script run again, and it diverges at call 0. In RunHost::publish (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs:289-298), removing `st.draft.base_version = p.version;` and `st.moved = true;` from the replay branch passes the suite, tests/resume.rs and tests/replay.rs included, though the step's `base` is then not recorded after a crash between a publish and the step's commit (History::of reads it at crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:598-600, and the next script loads its draft from it at script.rs:552-553). Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED. The same lines on the first run are held (steps.thread.json and steps.brief.json line 55, `\"base\": 2`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1352},"end":{"line":1387},"content_hash":"d4dc994bab133425a1d78341253c2958e1856e1fb1093ad58265159c53808a48"},"suggested_fix":"A run whose script publishes, crashed before the step commits (tests/resume.rs crashed_run), resumed: pin the step's payload and the journal across the crash.","summary":"A publish answered from the journal is not pinned: a replayed publish that leaves the draft's base where it was passes the suite","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:44:30.869045Z","id":"28ac5e85532f797c7a840a7e4591564a2783f98007b1ca8568c79838c6a4aac7","body":{"detail":"`named` strips `ending.`, `script.` or `answer.` and `.json` and looks for the rest as `\"stem\"` anywhere in the code, so a file is named by a string of another prefix (`\"pause-turn\"` names ending.pause-turn.json and script.pause-turn.json as well as answer.pause-turn.json) or by any literal equal to its stem (`\"done\"`, `\"fetch\"`, `\"Edit\"`), and by a pin in a test that is `#[ignore]`d or not compiled. A pin whose name is built (`format!`) or lives in another module reports its goldens as unnamed, which fails loudly; splitting this file breaks the check until it reads every part.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":2021},"end":{"line":2059},"content_hash":"2ca84f61ebb8bfa33f1b71d00ae6ac5a488d5f7444c80053844ff48efb7d21ae"},"suggested_fix":"Name every golden through one function that takes the file name and records it (or a const table of names the pins index), and compare that set with the directory.","summary":"every_golden_is_named_by_a_pin reads this file's text: any string that ends with a golden's stem names it, and a pin moved to another file names nothing","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:44:30.869053Z","id":"da9b54fb821ba2dfa720522eb593bd85c9234ad8a5aa79a6c5dac9422d7fac9d","body":{"detail":"(1) Split by the file's own sections: the Pins type, scrub and the run helpers (lines 107-416); runs (thread, brief, web: 418-595, 1947-2015); endings (597-1007); answers (1009-1159); script results (1161-1486); the web (1488-1945). (2) Two ways to compare: Pins::pin, and support::mismatch with `tests/golden/` and `p.text` written out 14 times; the three run tests name their ending golden by hand in both the `what` and the path where pin_ending builds both. A Pins::mismatch(what, name, value) would leave one. (3) run_on_both_threads (389-416) repeats Env::run_with_web's settings (tests/common/mod.rs:646-660) and NewRun; `set` (1678) is a second name beside free_weekly (370) and the inline set_bot_settings at 998-1003, and reads like Env::set, which sets RunSettings. (4) fetched (631) and fetched_then's URL (645) serve the web section 850 lines on, where GIVEN (1492) is the same URL and FETCH (1696) spells it a third time. (5) a_result_that_does_not_fit_is_cut (1326-1350) repeats pin_script's run. (6) web_refusals_are_pinned is one test of 240 lines and 16 runs; its cases as a table of (name, shape, code, setup) would read as the doc comment does. (7) Pins::ending gives a notice's place twice (`seq` and `after_notice_seq`).","kind":"suggestion","summary":"golden.rs is 2,059 lines holding six kinds of pin, two ways to compare, and helpers that repeat the tests' common module","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.043930Z","id":"9f2925b82f89437c5fcdbaf547ff81e19b35c56dbaeb550dae08043299b91401","body":{"detail":"Pins::writes and Pins::ending in crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/pins.rs read FakeState::writes (key `<run>:<step>:<seq>`, operation, thread). Both reversals of the threads in notify_at (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs) now fail six goldens. `.iter().rev().enumerate()`: tests/golden/ending.stopped.run-cap.two-threads.json line 70, after `\"key\": \"<run>:3:1000000\"`, golden `\"thread\": \"<thread-1>\"`, now `\"thread\": \"<thread-2>\"`. `.iter().enumerate().rev()`: the same golden line 68, after `\"writes_in_order\": [`, golden `\"key\": \"<run>:3:1000000\"`, now `\"key\": \"<run>:3:1000001\"`. The other five: ending.failed.two-threads, ending.give-up.two-threads, ending.finish.no-reply.two-threads, ending.finish.no-reply.two-threads.sources, ending.finish.replied-on-one-of-two-threads.sources. Command for each: the change made alone in crates/clax-bot/src, then `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh, then the change undone. Not closed: proposed to the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"d17b70dfda2e90eac8b4916617bf9b217d8e859689ebf48f485a9ae0d4de71c3","summary":"Pinned: every ending golden now holds the fake host's committed writes in order, each reply with its thread and journal place (writes_in_order)","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.044932Z","id":"38f3a3a2ed3c254436595d8eacfd8c48593cb2c6542247ee8ecea3343604f7fc","body":{"detail":"FakeBotHost::working (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs) pushes a FakeWorking {on, status, step} to FakeState::roster beside FakeState::working, which is unchanged. Pins::roster (crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/pins.rs) pins, in place of the list of calls: shown_working_before (for each step, whether a `true` call was made while the run was at it and not ended; the count is not pinned), shown_working_at_no_step, and stopped_showing (each `false` call with run_status and calls_after_it). working(false) moved before the commit in give_up fails six goldens: tests/golden/ending.give-up.context-window.json line 42, golden `\"run_status\": \"gave_up\"`, now `\"run_status\": \"running\"`; in finish it fails twelve: tests/golden/ending.finish.no-reply.sources.json line 57, golden `\"run_status\": \"finished\"`, now `\"run_status\": \"running\"`. The normalised form still fails for: working(true) on step 1 only (19 goldens, e.g. ending.give-up.no-tool-call.json line 35, `\"shown\": true` now false); working(false) twice in finish (12, ending.finish.no-reply.sources.json line 56, `\"calls_after_it\": 0` now 1); working(true) before must_stop (11, ending.stopped.cancelled.json line 17, `\"shown\": false` now true). Command for each: the change made alone in crates/clax-bot/src, then `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh, then the change undone. Not closed: proposed to the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"9655610a5a1a53b96284b5dba4d2c8b8de4d88ba354f95ae9e24c5a6c39b2d57","summary":"Pinned: the fake host records the run's status and step in the store at each working call, and an ending's roster holds the status at the call that stopped showing ClaxBot","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.045813Z","id":"2c442743dabdb02df3fd4df17cb8aba160ded0499dcd708869a705eb6fc67f82","body":{"detail":"Pins::script_calls (crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/pins.rs), pinned by the three tests of crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/scripts.rs. All six changes now fail. files.write not journaled: tests/golden/calls.draft-rebase.json line 27 (the journal of step 2 ends after files.replace) and calls.draft-operations.json. draft.rebase journaled without its value: calls.draft-rebase.json line 172, after `\"op\": \"draft.rebase\"`, golden `\"result\": {`, now `\"result\": null,`. A refused publish not journaled: calls.draft-rebase.json line 159 and calls.draft-operations.json line 488. A rules refusal not journaled: calls.draft-operations.json line 416 and calls.artifact-created-once.json line 29. Target of draft.rebase None: calls.draft-rebase.json line 74, golden `\"target\": \"<artifact>\"`, now `\"target\": null`. Target of files.write None: calls.draft-operations.json line 51, golden `\"target\": \"extra.css\"`, now null. tests/golden/resumed.rebase-publish-fetch.json fails for four of the six as well. Command for each: the change made alone in crates/clax-bot/src, then `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh, then the change undone. Not closed: proposed to the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"8edda3bc9d9bedabe3da147ab03e2f18f3a8765149d4b8c53dad1d93372c228e","summary":"Pinned: calls.draft-operations.json, calls.draft-rebase.json and calls.artifact-created-once.json hold each script step's `calls` and its journal rows","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.046651Z","id":"41901c5d58fdb35e9a51b3d50dd0bd18cd6a4d155f616da6dc47b724618764bc","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/endings.rs: finish_lists_the_sources_after_its_summary_on_every_thread, and finish_posts_its_summary_when_the_only_reply_came_before_a_publish (three scripts: one writes a file, one replies, one publishes; the test asserts the third's `changed` is empty and its `published` is version 2). Posting `{summary}{list}` on the first thread only fails tests/golden/ending.finish.no-reply.two-threads.sources.json line 21 (after `\"seq\": 1000000`, `\"step\": 4`: the second notice is gone). `wrote` without `|| !p[\"published\"].is_null()` fails tests/golden/ending.finish.replied-before-a-publish.json line 5, golden `\"posted\": true,`, now `\"posted\": false,`. Command for each: the change made alone in crates/clax-bot/src, then `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh, then the change undone. Not closed: proposed to the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"a71508ec56fc31b9b61354023cf879bcf316f7c2da8f2a2b4c0c4cae1669744b","summary":"Pinned: ending.finish.no-reply.two-threads.sources.json and ending.finish.replied-before-a-publish.json","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.047515Z","id":"e2845993c7c53d5666483a72fc719f843fa9fd10a1b032d8e883419c69c149bb","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/answers.rs, the_turn_after_a_paused_one_is_merged_into_its_message (pin_answer takes the turns before the finish and pins the last request). Merged blocks put first (`m.content.splice(0..0, content)`) fails tests/golden/answer.pause-turn.then-no-tool-call.json line 5, golden `\"text\": \"Working on it.\",`, now `\"text\": \"The heading is fine.\",`. No merging fails it at line 7 (the first message ends after one block), beside the unit test run::tests::history_merges_consecutive_turns_of_one_role. A nudge left out of History::of now fails goldens and no assertion before them: tests/golden/request.thread.4-after-no-tool-call.json line 73 and request.thread.4.wire.json byte 2629. Command for each: the change made alone in crates/clax-bot/src, then `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh, then the change undone. Not closed: proposed to the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"1d7d88c87843a707187cb5b5e376f18c546ed98b5287e85206e0669d30c044f2","summary":"Pinned: answer.pause-turn.then-no-tool-call.json is the third request of a run of a paused turn, a turn with no tool call and a finish","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.048388Z","id":"4f491b8a70948b846faa84bdda0dfcaec7fac5494bdc48e43b8b8e5361fc6137","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/resumed.rs: the driver dies at CrashPoint::BeforeCommit of the script step (crash_once of crates/clax-bot/tests/resume.rs), a second driver resumes after the claim lapses. Pinned: the step as stored, the run's journal, the fake host's writes; and the test asserts they equal those of the same script in a run without a crash, but for the step's attempt and commit time. One script edits, publishes and replies (tests/runs.rs EDIT); the other writes, rebases onto a version published before the run, publishes, replies and fetches. Removing `st.draft.base_version = p.version;` and `st.moved = true;` from the replay branch of RunHost::publish (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs) fails tests/golden/resumed.publish.json line 54, golden `\"base\": 2,`, now `\"base\": null,`, and tests/golden/resumed.rebase-publish-fetch.json line 106, golden `\"base\": 3,`, now `\"base\": 2,`. Command for each: the change made alone in crates/clax-bot/src, then `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh, then the change undone. Not closed: proposed to the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"7c5dd6f497da45c2a97d3d2c1cda745016e45385947cf31af584e176626a4f11","summary":"Pinned: resumed.publish.json and resumed.rebase-publish-fetch.json are a script crashed before its step's commit and run again, compared with the same script uncrashed","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.049229Z","id":"e4aa99a16efaed85252a4f3b28a817b5a4a879836f5f0a38def473a19fc788f8","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/names.rs: Golden's field is private, so only the `goldens!` table makes one and no pin can build a name; names::the_table_names_every_file_of_tests_golden compares the table with the `.json` files of tests/golden/ both ways. With a file `ending.stray.json` added and answer.pause-turn.json moved away it fails with `Files the table does not name ...: [\"ending.stray.json\"]` and `Goldens of the table with no file ...: [\"answer.pause-turn.json\"]`. What the test run does not catch: a table entry with a file that no pin takes. That is an unused constant, which the lint catches: with `NOT_PINNED = \"not-pinned.json\";` added, `bazel build --config=clippy //crates/clax-bot:integration` fails with `error: constant `NOT_PINNED` is never used`. A pin in a test that is `#[ignore]`d still counts as named. Not closed: proposed to the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"28ac5e85532f797c7a840a7e4591564a2783f98007b1ca8568c79838c6a4aac7","summary":"Replaced: every pin takes a Golden constant of the table in tests/golden/names.rs, and the table is compared with the directory","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.050081Z","id":"691716c7441446e15d75ac110784102dfbcd5f94f8ab4546cf666e87421abd45","body":{"detail":"(1) crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs declares names, pins, runs, endings, answers, scripts, web and resumed, beside the goldens in tests/golden/ (the split was made with the 73 goldens then in the directory unchanged). (2) Pins::pin for one golden and Pins::pin_all for several (Pins::json, Pins::wire, Pins::ending_pinned make the comparisons); no test writes a path or calls the helper. (3) Env::run_on_both_threads and Env::admin_sets in tests/common/mod.rs replace run_on_both_threads, `set` and the inline set_bot_settings; free_weekly is one line over admin_sets in endings.rs. (4) pins::GIVEN is the one fetched URL; web.rs builds its fetch line from it. (5) a_result_that_does_not_fit_is_cut uses scripts::script_run. (6) web.rs: refusals() is a table of Case {name, shape, code, before, source, mid}. (7) A notice's place is `seq` alone. Also: the golden's own EDIT script was a copy of tests/runs.rs EDIT and is now that constant; src/golden.rs's tests are src/golden_tests.rs, compiled by the library's tests alone. Not closed: proposed to the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"da9b54fb821ba2dfa720522eb593bd85c9234ad8a5aa79a6c5dac9422d7fac9d","summary":"Done, by the record's numbers: tests/golden.rs is the header and eight modules in tests/golden/, with one way to compare","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:21:33.253873Z","id":"559f9ff5a91696720b5033df081a4dcb95c839396831ff872dfc5573739a91bf","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"49ba727017e44f0127dceda958e0fe4c7a2aacdee079797bd2f3f7c30d7b28df","summary":"Not addressed here; the test this is pinned to moved: web_refusals_are_pinned and its table of cases (refusals) are now in crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/web.rs, so the span 1698:1707 of tests/golden.rs no longer exists. The suggestion stands as written.","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T06:30:12.630310Z","id":"74ea16817f238aaf61faf5065cfb53a180fc674737b97c6b0b675642d1b4c306","body":{"detail":"`ClaxSession` calls what crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs calls (`Draft`, `check::check`, `BotHost::plan_publish` and `plan_write`, `run_plan`, `api::target`), but the order between those calls (`policy` 199-225, `draft_op` 227-280, `publish` 282-341, the tracking at 442-449) is written again, since today's are methods of `RunHost` over a `Tick`. Until script.rs is moved behind the seam there are two copies; the tests of this file fail only if they come apart in what three scripts leave. A declared `web.*` call is refused by the adapter (`Performer::Web`), and its `ending` and `ended` do nothing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":438},"content_hash":"55b0af0bd6469bc6d3e580020e74ed5cc7f609a5fdd91fb24bd027f2794b0251"},"summary":"The test adapter writes the glue of `RunHost` a second time, and leaves out the web performer and the endings","tags":["seam","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T06:47:34.697051Z","id":"b532511714bb4dafc1ed03a772fd7ceea8e19e5e49d0673af596155c93451baa","body":{"detail":"`Left` compares a step's journal rows (step, attempt, seq, op, ok, result), the fake host's writes by key and operation (a reply's thread also), the calls that reached it, the script's value, the step's `calls` without `ms`, five payload fields, `published` in the tool result, and the stored draft. Not compared: a journal row's `args_hash`; a write's arguments (a reply's body, a publish's note, addresses and files; the published version's files); the rest of the tool result and of the payload (`result`, `outcome`, `tool_use_id`); the events emitted; the audit records (`bot.script`, `bot.call` and its `replayed`); usage. `Stepper` (446-515) builds none of those and asserts on a diverged replay instead of answering it. No script here has a refused publish, a write the host's plan refuses, a publish without `addresses`, a cancelled script (`StepEnd::Cancelled` is never passed) or a declared web call. Each of these was made, one at a time, to `ClaxSession` and then to crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, and `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::` passed all three tests: a refused publish not journaled (seam.rs 339; script.rs 399-401); a host write refused by its plan not journaled (seam.rs 362; script.rs 422-424); the publish's `note` dropped (seam.rs 324; script.rs 327); the default `addresses` dropped (seam.rs 313; script.rs 315). Nine others failed on both sides, as they should: a draft operation journaled with its value, a policy refusal not journaled, a replayed host write or publish reaching the host, `published` missing from the tool result, a draft row dropped on the replayed attempt, a replayed publish not moving the draft, a replayed reply not counted, a replayed rebase going to the current version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":656},"end":{"line":712},"content_hash":"46068fd5ad2bf154994217c5d219a6c77ce6db83be671d4d6ed2c87dbcc3dc77"},"suggested_fix":"Before script.rs moves: add a script whose publish is refused (`conflict`, someone published first) and whose host write is refused by the plan (`FakeState::fail_next`), one that publishes with no `addresses`, and a cancelled one; and compare the writes' arguments.","summary":"What the proof of the seam does not compare, and four changes, made to the adapter and to today's code alike, that it does not notice","tags":["review","seam","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T07:16:53.196680Z","id":"ac6f1295715fcc9dbbc31eea26e56c388e9348e26b082dcbb0aa1ba69e4b3986","body":{"detail":"`Left` (seam.rs 623) adds `written` (each host write with its arguments: a reply's thread and body, a publish's note and addresses), `drafts` (each `PublishDraft` the fake host was given: files with contents, `if_version`, note, addresses), `versions` (the store's versions past the first: note, files, content hash), `error` (the kind the script ended with) and `web_records`. New tests: `refused_writes_behind_a_session_are_journaled_and_not_asked_of_the_host_again` (1152: a publish refused `conflict`, a `threads.reply` refused at `plan_write` by `FakeState::fail_next`, a `db.update` of a missing document whose plan fails in its transaction after `plan_write` succeeded, then a reply that succeeds; it requires one journal row for each, written by attempt 1, and each call to have reached the host once); `a_publish_that_names_no_threads_addresses_the_runs` (1106); `a_cancelled_script_behind_a_session_keeps_what_todays_run_loop_keeps` (1435: the stopped step keeps `published`, `replied`, `base` alone, no draft row, and what was published and replied stands). Mutations, one at a time, `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::`, 7 tests: (1) refused publish not journaled: adapter (`Answer::written(Err(e))` at seam.rs 360) fails `refused_writes…`; script.rs 400 removed fails the same test. (2) host write refused by its plan not journaled: adapter (seam.rs 386) and script.rs 423 each fail `refused_writes…`. (3) publish's `note` dropped: adapter (seam.rs 345) and script.rs 327 each fail four tests (`a_replayed_publish…`, `a_replayed_rebase…`, `a_publish_that_names_no_threads…`, `a_cancelled_script…`). (4) default `addresses` dropped: adapter (seam.rs 334) and script.rs 315 each fail `a_publish_that_names_no_threads…` and `a_cancelled_script…`. All seven pass unmutated. Still not compared: a journal row's `args_hash`, the rest of the tool result and payload, events, audit records other than the `bot.web` count, usage; `Stepper` still stops on a diverged replay. One limit found: the fake host does not store a version's addresses (`Version::addresses` is empty for its versions), so addresses are compared through the draft the host was given, not the stored version.","kind":"comment","references":"b532511714bb4dafc1ed03a772fd7ceea8e19e5e49d0673af596155c93451baa","span":{"start":{"line":1004},"end":{"line":1310},"content_hash":"9c7efdf855ffdd6144625fb0c42f9b7427dcc371d70339ccc7b58353dd0f1f32"},"summary":"The proof now has the four scripts and compares the writes' arguments; each of the four changes, made to the adapter and to script.rs, now fails a seam test","tags":["seam","fix-round","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T07:16:53.200751Z","id":"0c7760fae8bc7f42446e2c511c422756c9443810f3f92e29a3bbf8d0ed028d66","body":{"detail":"`ClaxSession::call` (seam.rs 398) answers `web_disabled` for `Performer::Web` through `web_disabled` (118), the same answer `undeclared` gives, so both halves of check 2 of crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs are behind the seam; checks 3 to 9 are not. Every call goes through `surface::dispatch` (`Stepper`, 485). The two copies of the glue remain until script.rs moves, and now fail seven tests instead of three when they come apart (record b5325117's four changes among them). `ending` and `ended` still do nothing.","kind":"comment","references":"74ea16817f238aaf61faf5065cfb53a180fc674737b97c6b0b675642d1b4c306","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"9813c8968fe50a23329498bc91a6b399e2541b3b1a6e2863264cdfda212ca872"},"summary":"The adapter now refuses a declared web operation as a host with no web source does, and is run through the conformance suite; its endings are still not carried","tags":["seam","fix-round","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T07:32:09.941709Z","id":"bafb6e2728db8db4c49853f042d190f02137101b3994887b98c9cbe91adee928","body":{"detail":"Every script the proof runs is step 2 of its run, after one turn: `tally` (seam.rs 102-111) always answers `(None, false)` and `begin` (145-163) always loads the draft at the run's own base. Changes made one at a time and run with `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::` (7 tests): (1) seam.rs 148 loads the draft at `run.base_version` whatever `tally` answers: all 7 pass. (2) seam.rs 238 drops `self.created_before`: all 7 pass. (3) seam.rs 320 never refuses a second publish in one script: all 7 pass. (4) seam.rs 215 hands `OpCtx::new` another attempt: all 7 pass (the fake host does not read it; crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs 633 does). The same changes made to today's code and run against the whole of `//crates/clax-bot:integration` (175 tests): script.rs 217 without `self.tick.hist.created` fails `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused` and `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact`; script.rs 301 fails `golden::scripts::the_draft_operations_answers_are_pinned`; but script.rs 554 as `let base = self.run.base_version;` passes all 175, the seam's 7 among them, and passes `//crates/clax-bot:all`, `//crates/clax-server:all` and `//crates/clax-worker:bot_test` too. No test runs a script after a step that published or rebased: crates/clax-bot/tests/rules.rs 143-197 rebases and publishes in the run's last script. So the change that moves script.rs 554-555 into a provider's `begin` can load every later script's draft at the run's first base (a second publish then conflicts, and a script after a rebase reads the old files) and pass the proof and every fixture under crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"2b972208ab43b6e12922b690053be2a951f2af8fcbd6f7948fdefb9b08f05372"},"suggested_fix":"A proof case, and a fixture for today's path, in which a first script publishes (and another in which it rebases) and a second script reads a file, writes and publishes: the second step's draft, its `if_version` and its `payload.base` compared on both paths. For a brief's run, a second script that calls `artifacts.create` after a first that created one.","summary":"No proof case opens a session over a history that moved the draft's base or created an artifact, so what `begin` folds from the committed steps is unproved, and for the base no other test of clax-bot holds it either","tags":["review","seam","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T07:59:36.786172Z","id":"51b21b23df995cfda3596f8c8207fa3ae1b8d0443e1f287a92eeba0de80ac724","body":{"detail":"`ClaxSession` calls what crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs calls (`Draft`, `check::check`, `BotHost::plan_publish` and `plan_write`, `run_plan`, `api::target`), but the order between those calls (`policy` 199-225, `draft_op` 227-280, `publish` 282-341, the tracking at 442-449) is written again, since today's are methods of `RunHost` over a `Tick`. Until script.rs is moved behind the seam there are two copies; the tests of this file fail only if they come apart in what three scripts leave. A declared `web.*` call is refused by the adapter (`Performer::Web`), and its `ending` and `ended` do nothing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":525},"content_hash":"287ba56af9ae4f1cbe9cdb2fd57c8d11bad61cfaf81c1314a29647775de3e6d3"},"summary":"The test adapter writes the glue of `RunHost` a second time, and leaves out the web performer and the endings","supersedes":"74ea16817f238aaf61faf5065cfb53a180fc674737b97c6b0b675642d1b4c306","tags":["seam","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T07:59:36.937126Z","id":"fd5ba3b8dee5f8c47f2082d41a20acb430e0c0ffa12f742b7138d2589ad960c3","body":{"detail":"`Left` compares a step's journal rows (step, attempt, seq, op, ok, result), the fake host's writes by key and operation (a reply's thread also), the calls that reached it, the script's value, the step's `calls` without `ms`, five payload fields, `published` in the tool result, and the stored draft. Not compared: a journal row's `args_hash`; a write's arguments (a reply's body, a publish's note, addresses and files; the published version's files); the rest of the tool result and of the payload (`result`, `outcome`, `tool_use_id`); the events emitted; the audit records (`bot.script`, `bot.call` and its `replayed`); usage. `Stepper` (446-515) builds none of those and asserts on a diverged replay instead of answering it. No script here has a refused publish, a write the host's plan refuses, a publish without `addresses`, a cancelled script (`StepEnd::Cancelled` is never passed) or a declared web call. Each of these was made, one at a time, to `ClaxSession` and then to crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, and `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::` passed all three tests: a refused publish not journaled (seam.rs 339; script.rs 399-401); a host write refused by its plan not journaled (seam.rs 362; script.rs 422-424); the publish's `note` dropped (seam.rs 324; script.rs 327); the default `addresses` dropped (seam.rs 313; script.rs 315). Nine others failed on both sides, as they should: a draft operation journaled with its value, a policy refusal not journaled, a replayed host write or publish reaching the host, `published` missing from the tool result, a draft row dropped on the replayed attempt, a replayed publish not moving the draft, a replayed reply not counted, a replayed rebase going to the current version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":791},"end":{"line":896},"content_hash":"26eab866e7929cb0ca2b02371e456b14111d3bfedca0e365086ea9c731167c72"},"suggested_fix":"Before script.rs moves: add a script whose publish is refused (`conflict`, someone published first) and whose host write is refused by the plan (`FakeState::fail_next`), one that publishes with no `addresses`, and a cancelled one; and compare the writes' arguments.","summary":"What the proof of the seam does not compare, and four changes, made to the adapter and to today's code alike, that it does not notice","supersedes":"b532511714bb4dafc1ed03a772fd7ceea8e19e5e49d0673af596155c93451baa","tags":["review","seam","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T07:59:48.071528Z","id":"de585b778b5fbddd831bd91086a7922719c5f567468e7f10a6fd0bb1c4b63235","body":{"detail":"Proof (crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs): `Case::following` (926) commits a first script through today's run loop on both paths, so the script compared is step 4 and its session is opened over a history. `a_script_after_a_publish_starts_from_the_published_version` (1505): the second script reads the first's edit, writes and publishes; it compares the whole of `Left` and requires the second draft's `if_version` to be 2, `payload.base` 3 and the stored draft's paths. `a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto` (1555): it reads their file and publishes over version 2. `a_script_after_one_that_created_an_artifact_may_not_create_another` (1582), a brief's run: the second `artifacts.create` is refused and does not reach the host. Today's path (crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/resumed.rs 180, 200): `resumed.second-script.after-a-publish.json` and `resumed.second-script.after-a-rebase.json` pin the second script's step, the drafts given to publish (`drafts_published`, with `if_version`), the journal, usage and audit, across a crash before that step's commit. Changes: seam.rs 170 loading the draft at `run.base_version` fails both seam tests of a later script; crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs 554 as `let base = self.run.base_version;` fails those two and both new fixtures' tests; seam.rs 260 without `self.created_before` fails the brief's test. Each change was made alone and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration` (189 tests) passes without it.","kind":"comment","references":"bafb6e2728db8db4c49853f042d190f02137101b3994887b98c9cbe91adee928","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"f1b59ad6382e9a4f9cdae00c64c09551e4bf3aea3ca60c7662dbf1178ead7f8e"},"summary":"The base and `created` a session folds from the committed steps are now proved against today's run loop and pinned for today's path; both changes that passed now fail","tags":["seam","fix-round","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T08:00:09.876023Z","id":"487f98c0e44495a0598f7656ff672e3ea4399c392ab86508349d72ea1547d28e","body":{"detail":"Every script the proof runs is step 2 of its run, after one turn: `tally` (seam.rs 102-111) always answers `(None, false)` and `begin` (145-163) always loads the draft at the run's own base. Changes made one at a time and run with `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::` (7 tests): (1) seam.rs 148 loads the draft at `run.base_version` whatever `tally` answers: all 7 pass. (2) seam.rs 238 drops `self.created_before`: all 7 pass. (3) seam.rs 320 never refuses a second publish in one script: all 7 pass. (4) seam.rs 215 hands `OpCtx::new` another attempt: all 7 pass (the fake host does not read it; crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs 633 does). The same changes made to today's code and run against the whole of `//crates/clax-bot:integration` (175 tests): script.rs 217 without `self.tick.hist.created` fails `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused` and `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact`; script.rs 301 fails `golden::scripts::the_draft_operations_answers_are_pinned`; but script.rs 554 as `let base = self.run.base_version;` passes all 175, the seam's 7 among them, and passes `//crates/clax-bot:all`, `//crates/clax-server:all` and `//crates/clax-worker:bot_test` too. No test runs a script after a step that published or rebased: crates/clax-bot/tests/rules.rs 143-197 rebases and publishes in the run's last script. So the change that moves script.rs 554-555 into a provider's `begin` can load every later script's draft at the run's first base (a second publish then conflicts, and a script after a rebase reads the old files) and pass the proof and every fixture under crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"f1b59ad6382e9a4f9cdae00c64c09551e4bf3aea3ca60c7662dbf1178ead7f8e"},"suggested_fix":"A proof case, and a fixture for today's path, in which a first script publishes (and another in which it rebases) and a second script reads a file, writes and publishes: the second step's draft, its `if_version` and its `payload.base` compared on both paths. For a brief's run, a second script that calls `artifacts.create` after a first that created one.","summary":"No proof case opens a session over a history that moved the draft's base or created an artifact, so what `begin` folds from the committed steps is unproved, and for the base no other test of clax-bot holds it either","supersedes":"bafb6e2728db8db4c49853f042d190f02137101b3994887b98c9cbe91adee928","tags":["review","seam","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T08:13:35.638575Z","id":"94986a8ad61f81c5f37f8ee6c08d6719bae690d9b0d27a42b6c84189f2053f44","body":{"detail":"`bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::` (12 tests), one change at a time: seam.rs 170 loading at `run.base_version` fails `a_script_after_a_publish_starts_from_the_published_version` and `a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto`; 260 without `created_before` fails `a_script_after_one_that_created_an_artifact_may_not_create_another`; 342 never refusing a second publish fails `a_replayed_host_read_and_a_second_publish_behind_a_session`; 237 with another attempt fails eight tests. crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs 554 as `let base = self.run.base_version;` against the whole target (189 tests) fails those two seam tests and `golden::resumed::a_script_after_a_publish_is_resumed_from_the_published_version` and `…after_a_rebase_is_resumed_from_the_version_rebased_onto`. Both new fixtures are of a run that crashed before the second script's commit, and `pin_resumed` (crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/resumed.rs 100-137) requires the same run without a crash to leave the same but for the step's attempt, its commit time and the audit records.","kind":"comment","references":"487f98c0e44495a0598f7656ff672e3ea4399c392ab86508349d72ea1547d28e","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"f1b59ad6382e9a4f9cdae00c64c09551e4bf3aea3ca60c7662dbf1178ead7f8e"},"summary":"Verified at 3b700b895: each of the four changes now fails a test, on the adapter and on today's path","tags":["seam","verified","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/policy.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T14:13:58.218358Z","id":"7e34a88715b26997796d45eeffe16271266b944181db00ca5aeb3ca2f6b0ce66","body":{"detail":"Each applied alone, then `bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot:all`; all pass with: (1) `Overflows::of` resetting `running` only on a step that is not a turn, so a turn that fits no longer starts the count over (the tests put a script between the overflows); (2) the in-tick retry guard `available().is_none_or(..)` as `is_some_and(..)`: no test retries with neither a budget nor a minutes cap; (3) `affordable` taking the run's whole credits cap as what is left: `a_cap_on_credits_the_policy_sets_keeps_a_turn_within_what_is_left` (policy.rs:235) accepts either branch and cannot tell the cap from what is left of it; (4) `too_short` with `<=` for `<`; (5) and (6) `overflowed` given `None` for `sent_bytes` on the refused and on the stop-reason path: no test overflows twice with a policy that answers the second ask as it answered the first; (7) a cap of the run loop's own added to `must_stop` as a literal (`committed >= 1000`), which the textual guard does not see; (8) the `context window` needle deleted; (9) `(400..500).contains(status)` as `*status < 500`; (10) `observe_every` not raised to 1 (a 0 then records no delta, and nothing panics). Killed: `>=` to `>` on the steps and credits caps, `remaining()` as `Some(0)` with no cap, `running` for `level` in either ask, `bytes_text(0)`, usage on a refused turn, `payload.shown` for `Shown::Core`, the description from `tool_result_bytes`, `>=` to `>` and the answer's blocks counted in `sent`, and the retries bound off by one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":694},"end":{"line":780}},"summary":"What the policy's tests do not hold: ten of twenty-two mutations of the run loop and the policy pass every test","tags":["review","verify-t4","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T13:49:41.851010Z","id":"f4313af2ad95b51999330cc9e2b5060093b2a5022b5d48b36d3496fb087b9527","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs 159: `let Tally { base, created, .. } = Tally::of(cx.history);` in place of the test's `tally` (which read every step with a payload; `Tally::of` reads every committed step, and `attempt` passes only committed steps, seam.rs 624-627). What the proof compares is unchanged, and `bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot:all` passes with it. The fold itself is unit-tested in crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 80-239 and compared with the old single fold in crates/clax-bot/src/history_reference.rs.","kind":"comment","references":"487f98c0e44495a0598f7656ff672e3ea4399c392ab86508349d72ea1547d28e","summary":"The adapter's own fold of the base and `created` is gone: `begin` calls `clax::Tally::of`, the function the run loop's tick calls, so the two cannot differ","tags":["t3","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/policy.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T14:58:17.900393Z","id":"e91ff03c20166955b36e39d5ed3defe8a8dd2816b2a4bae33b230a353fbd3400","body":{"detail":"Applied one at a time, then `bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot:all`: (1) fails `a_step_that_fits_starts_the_count_of_overflows_over` and the unit test of `Overflows::of` (a turn alone between two overflows); (2) `a_failed_call_is_made_again_in_the_tick_of_a_run_with_no_bound`; (3) `a_cap_on_credits_keeps_a_turn_within_what_the_run_has_left_of_it` (a first turn of 400,000 tokens, then a cap 21 credits over what was spent: `max_tokens` is within what that pays for); (4) `a_cap_on_minutes_the_policy_sets_is_the_one_that_stops_the_run` (exactly a minute left: the turn is taken); (5) and (6) `a_policy_that_repeats_its_answer_on_the_next_overflow_ends_the_run`, on each path; (7) `a_run_with_no_bound_goes_far_past_every_default`; (8) `each_phrase_alone_says_a_request_is_too_long`; (9) `only_a_refusal_with_a_4xx_status_is_one_for_length`; (10) is gone as a mutation: `RunLimits::observe_every` is a `NonZeroUsize`, and its default is held by `the_settings_limits_are_their_caps_and_the_default_sizes`. The effect of `observe_every` on what a crashed attempt is charged is still not held by a run (an attempt's entry replaces its last, crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs:1429-1432).","kind":"comment","references":"7e34a88715b26997796d45eeffe16271266b944181db00ca5aeb3ca2f6b0ce66","span":{"start":{"line":694},"end":{"line":780},"content_hash":"a403341cfae6266655be4ebbaf668ca11d350128ce749efe451338d10e473e27"},"summary":"Each of the ten now fails a test, and `observe_every` cannot be 0","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/policy.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T15:19:27.111255Z","id":"63b88abd101c2600eabc1e80c4e52920807acd39ac118162a9c4f39587fe6874","body":{"detail":"The 21 earlier mutations that still apply (the one on `observe_every` cannot be written against a `NonZeroUsize`) each fail a test now, the literal cap in `must_stop` by `a_run_with_no_bound_goes_far_past_every_default`. Of 18 new ones, 17 fail a test: the hash comparison dropped; the core's projection accepted after an overflow; the allowance of `check_shortened` given to any paused turn; the policy's failures bound off by one; the cancel not read while the policy fails; a `finish` not taken while it fails; a shortened history priced with a cached prefix; `unbounded` keeping the minutes cap; `unbounded` setting a model call's timeout; `is_overflow` not asked on the refused path; the instance's caps applied while the policy fails; `overflow_ending` taking the other path's ending; a timed-out call waiting; the first turn's request check dropped; a policy's messages not checked; a commit's failures named `policy_error`; an `Err` on an overflow's ask taken for a shorter history. Passing every test: the guard `model_call_timeout.is_some_and(|t| t.is_zero())` in `turn` removed. The call is then made with a total of zero, is cut before it is sent and retried, and the run stops `model_timeout` all the same; only the open turn's attempts differ. `a_model_call_that_outlasts_the_policys_timeout_stops_the_run` passed 60 runs of 60 under load; its 20 ms bound must still outlast the request reaching the fake provider for `requests().len() == 2` to hold.","kind":"comment","references":"7e34a88715b26997796d45eeffe16271266b944181db00ca5aeb3ca2f6b0ce66","summary":"Run again on the fixed code: 38 of 39 mutations fail a test, among them the nine that passed before and can still be written; the one that passes is close to equivalent","tags":["review","verify-t4","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/policy.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T15:19:27.111409Z","id":"6dac8428706e33c79f510b74eb7e04ed8ef86e8fcc398bb1af88f2839e7eba16","body":{"detail":"`seed_a_long_run` opens the test database beside the store's connection and inserts into `bot_steps (run_id, n, kind, started_at, committed_at, payload_json)` and updates `bot_runs.credits_milli`. A renamed or dropped column, or a new one that is `NOT NULL` with no default, fails the test loudly (the statements are unwrapped); a new column the run loop reads and a tick always sets would be absent on the seeded rows and read as its default, silently. The seeded turns are `pause_turn`s with no `assistant` blocks and an empty `usage`, which a tick does not write, and the run's credits have no usage rows behind them (the ledger and `credits_milli` disagree by 100,000 credits). The folds read them as a run of 5,000 committed steps whose transcript is the request alone, so the test holds that no count of steps, credits or days stops a run, and its own documentation says it does not see a bound on a history's size. The person is `claxbot_unenforced`, so `affordable` returns before the week's credits are read; `a_run_with_no_cap_on_credits_spends_past_the_settings_and_finishes` covers that path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":554},"end":{"line":592},"content_hash":"c65bd90191aee06d6bb5c665a229872df49743a858004c8c7f19e5582d9aa0a1"},"suggested_fix":"If the store gains a way to commit a step without a tick (as its own tests do with `begin_step` and `commit_step`), seed through it so a migration cannot pass this test by; until then the SQL is a fair price for a test that 5,000 ticks would make slow.","summary":"The run of 5,000 steps is written by SQL that names the store's columns, with turns no tick writes and no usage rows: what it holds, and what a schema change does to it","tags":["review","verify-t4","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/policy.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T15:26:27.763248Z","id":"7475b1bda257f32b7d0b7ec92ee3ae5b7f0d19cde3b5d5c04d74afbb108f4e46","body":{"detail":"`seed_a_long_run` opens the test database beside the store's connection and inserts into `bot_steps (run_id, n, kind, started_at, committed_at, payload_json)` and updates `bot_runs.credits_milli`. A renamed or dropped column, or a new one that is `NOT NULL` with no default, fails the test loudly (the statements are unwrapped); a new column the run loop reads and a tick always sets would be absent on the seeded rows and read as its default, silently. The seeded turns are `pause_turn`s with no `assistant` blocks and an empty `usage`, which a tick does not write, and the run's credits have no usage rows behind them (the ledger and `credits_milli` disagree by 100,000 credits). The folds read them as a run of 5,000 committed steps whose transcript is the request alone, so the test holds that no count of steps, credits or days stops a run, and its own documentation says it does not see a bound on a history's size. The person is `claxbot_unenforced`, so `affordable` returns before the week's credits are read; `a_run_with_no_cap_on_credits_spends_past_the_settings_and_finishes` covers that path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":578},"end":{"line":616},"content_hash":"c65bd90191aee06d6bb5c665a229872df49743a858004c8c7f19e5582d9aa0a1"},"suggested_fix":"If the store gains a way to commit a step without a tick (as its own tests do with `begin_step` and `commit_step`), seed through it so a migration cannot pass this test by; until then the SQL is a fair price for a test that 5,000 ticks would make slow.","summary":"The run of 5,000 steps is written by SQL that names the store's columns, with turns no tick writes and no usage rows: what it holds, and what a schema change does to it","supersedes":"6dac8428706e33c79f510b74eb7e04ed8ef86e8fcc398bb1af88f2839e7eba16","tags":["review","verify-t4","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/policy.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T15:26:34.616347Z","id":"b29ef3e0958e93881b6cfd9d86e8783247192a0279c7e115291973c3efac051b","body":{"detail":"Applied one at a time, then `bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot:all`: (1) fails `a_step_that_fits_starts_the_count_of_overflows_over` and the unit test of `Overflows::of` (a turn alone between two overflows); (2) `a_failed_call_is_made_again_in_the_tick_of_a_run_with_no_bound`; (3) `a_cap_on_credits_keeps_a_turn_within_what_the_run_has_left_of_it` (a first turn of 400,000 tokens, then a cap 21 credits over what was spent: `max_tokens` is within what that pays for); (4) `a_cap_on_minutes_the_policy_sets_is_the_one_that_stops_the_run` (exactly a minute left: the turn is taken); (5) and (6) `a_policy_that_repeats_its_answer_on_the_next_overflow_ends_the_run`, on each path; (7) `a_run_with_no_bound_goes_far_past_every_default`; (8) `each_phrase_alone_says_a_request_is_too_long`; (9) `only_a_refusal_with_a_4xx_status_is_one_for_length`; (10) is gone as a mutation: `RunLimits::observe_every` is a `NonZeroUsize`, and its default is held by `the_settings_limits_are_their_caps_and_the_default_sizes`. The effect of `observe_every` on what a crashed attempt is charged is still not held by a run (an attempt's entry replaces its last, crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs:1429-1432).","kind":"comment","references":"7e34a88715b26997796d45eeffe16271266b944181db00ca5aeb3ca2f6b0ce66","span":{"start":{"line":718},"end":{"line":804},"content_hash":"a403341cfae6266655be4ebbaf668ca11d350128ce749efe451338d10e473e27"},"summary":"Each of the ten now fails a test, and `observe_every` cannot be 0","supersedes":"e91ff03c20166955b36e39d5ed3defe8a8dd2816b2a4bae33b230a353fbd3400","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/policy.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T15:27:12.275521Z","id":"d6b765e371e42d98ca6a96f120ea47513a10d769235dc31c52325bb5494853c9","body":{"detail":"`seed_a_long_run` rewritten to claim the run and call `Store::begin_step_on` and `Store::commit_bot_step` 5,000 times, each commit charging 15,000 output tokens (so the credits were real usage rows), ran in 6.61 s (`SEEDED in 6.612942375s`, from `bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=a_run_with_no_bound --test_arg=--nocapture`, fastbuild); the test passed that way too. The whole integration suite takes about 9 s, so that one helper would nearly double it. The SQL version is kept. What would make the store's path affordable is a store call that commits many steps in one transaction, which is the store's to add; until then a column renamed in `bot_steps` or `bot_runs.credits_milli` fails this test at its `INSERT`, loudly, and a column added with a default changes nothing it holds.","kind":"comment","references":"7475b1bda257f32b7d0b7ec92ee3ae5b7f0d19cde3b5d5c04d74afbb108f4e46","span":{"start":{"line":578},"end":{"line":616},"content_hash":"c65bd90191aee06d6bb5c665a229872df49743a858004c8c7f19e5582d9aa0a1"},"summary":"Seeding through the store's own calls was tried and is too slow: 5,000 steps took 6.6 s, so the SQL stays","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.592341Z","id":"c00da07a114cd4f4f91fc3ddd7475b3c6a64bd37e290e0a4abc3beee0154e904","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs builds `clax_bot::clax::ClaxProvider` and drives it through its own `Stepper` against `clax_bot::tick`, which runs the same provider through crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs. So the proof now holds one provider under two drivers, not two copies of the operations. The web operations are whole in the provider (clax/web.rs), and the proof has a case of calls that reach the source and are replayed. `ending` and `ended` still do nothing. What compares the provider with the code it replaced is crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs.","kind":"comment","references":"51b21b23df995cfda3596f8c8207fa3ae1b8d0443e1f287a92eeba0de80ac724","summary":"The adapter is gone: there is one copy of the glue, the product's, and the proof drives it","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.592997Z","id":"2085f840b36966ae69f9fc76f3b05e989df4691784dfd2533c94135a880d275f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs drives twenty runs through the reference (src/script_reference.rs) and through the seam and compares every step as stored (the whole payload: `result`, `outcome`, `tool_use_id`), every journal row, the live events, the `bot.*` audit records, the usage rows, the host's writes with their arguments, the calls that reached it with their attempts, the drafts published, the versions, the replies, the stored draft, the web source's calls and the pages kept. A row's `args_hash` is compared as which rows of the run share it (the arguments hold a home's own IDs), and its value by runs resumed across the two codes, where a hash the other code did not expect would diverge. The proof's `Left` is as it was: it cannot reach the reference, which is compiled for the library's tests alone.","kind":"comment","references":"fd5ba3b8dee5f8c47f2082d41a20acb430e0c0ffa12f742b7138d2589ad960c3","summary":"What `Left` lacks is compared where the old code can be run: the library's unit tests, over whole runs","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.596873Z","id":"69ec4c593dce7091b8581ff6b680647bafe51ff085d54dbe6da7b5742c082fe5","body":{"detail":"Since the run loop runs a script's calls through `ClaxProvider`, both sides of every comparison in this file are that provider: once through this file's `Stepper`, once through crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs. A fault in the provider that both drivers meet the same way passes it. What compares the provider with the old code is crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, and what pins the values is the goldens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":27},"content_hash":"5087b821ae9a9b56560882e5960d152e69da8c3d52ece25661ed5d683e39943e"},"summary":"The proof compares one provider under two drivers, no longer the seam with the code it replaced","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:16:38.555271Z","id":"79e2c3250a4a689c28d2a26429aa1c858506a0685c641f3ea513f5b3962839ec","body":{"detail":"`RacedToThePage` writes, from inside the source's fetch, a journal row and a page of the same URL at place 500 of the open step (`Store::spend_journaled`, with the driver the test minted), so the fetch under way is refused `page_exists`. The store has no hook to fail one write or one read: a provider's conformance fixture, which is not given the driver, cannot make `clax` answer `Answer::unwritten` (crates/clax-bot/tests/providers.rs names the case not applicable), and the committed half of record 785c9e30 (a read of the run's row failing with the claim held) cannot be driven at all. A `fail_next` on the tests' store, as `FakeBotHost` has, would let both be played.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1673},"end":{"line":1678},"content_hash":"2fec9d3eac3005fdf2b0c5ba4c711ae2345338856fa203a5ce540910f4886c24"},"summary":"The one test of a web transaction the store refuses makes it fail by a page kept at another place of the same step, which takes the driver's ID","tags":["t5","fix-round","for-t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:07:27.535940Z","id":"0e0d27a8ffd71eb7ea8bdb80b49fc2757ff8b26b5821531fad34b2b4c5baadeb","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"79e2c3250a4a689c28d2a26429aa1c858506a0685c641f3ea513f5b3962839ec","summary":"Not changed: the test still fails the transaction the same way. Its neighbours that dropped or replaced the web source by writing `deps.web` now call `Deps::without_web` and `Deps::with_web`","tags":["t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/outside.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T21:35:40.598681Z","id":"db9b99ab77d9d64b789813b618aa442b31381f02bdac0c95d59241a1322d7498","body":{"detail":"Not done for two reasons. No test of clax-bot depends on clax-testkit, which depends on clax-server: the dev-dependency is allowed (scripts/check-crate-layers.py does not check them, and bazel/cargo.bzl keeps the testkit out of unit tests), but it would put the whole daemon under this crate's integration test. And `MemoryHub` (crates/clax-testkit/src/fake_host/memory.rs) keeps its `Hub` and `MemoryPending` private, so a `HubBroker` cannot share them; it would have to be rebuilt over `HubBroker::with`. `Host` here serves the hub with the protocol's own messages (`clax_surface::wire`) and counts each key it performed, which is what the tests read of a host.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"e5699afa92070818567a4a6445cc7f9d0a748e69e1a8d7f0e94656a647e10dec"},"summary":"Drive the in-process runs with clax-testkit's FakeHost and MemoryHub in place of this file's scripted host","tags":["revisit:MemoryHub is built over HubBroker, or the daemon's end-to-end test needs the same host in process","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/outside.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T21:35:40.598714Z","id":"58c11eaab393884959c2c2de7cfc06669946adda9ed6c7ea3e86a276de9bd6e8","body":{"detail":"`no_source_of_the_run_loop_names_the_fixtures_surface` reads `src` of clax-bot and the crates it depends on (clax-bot-sandbox, clax-core, clax-rt, clax-sample, clax-store, clax-surface), which its Bazel target is given as test data (crates/clax-bot/BUILD.bazel). clax-http, clax-server, clax-worker and the rest are above this crate: giving their sources to this test would rerun it on every change to them. The daemon's end-to-end test is where the scan of every crate belongs. Test files (`tests.rs`, a `tests` directory, what follows `#[cfg(test)]`) are skipped: crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs replays the fixture and names its surface.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1031},"end":{"line":1039},"content_hash":"286dd4e0ed8dbe3373c0a159df21e0779e828d1310ddc3c8a65004190811918c"},"summary":"The scan for the fixture's surface name reads the run loop's crates only, not the daemon's","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/outside.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.310298Z","id":"2e2acc88e9025fe217976ba91f6e9917069093ac9ee3d3c29e9a626eca92ec35","body":{"detail":"Not done for two reasons. No test of clax-bot depends on clax-testkit, which depends on clax-server: the dev-dependency is allowed (scripts/check-crate-layers.py does not check them, and bazel/cargo.bzl keeps the testkit out of unit tests), but it would put the whole daemon under this crate's integration test. And `MemoryHub` (crates/clax-testkit/src/fake_host/memory.rs) keeps its `Hub` and `MemoryPending` private, so a `HubBroker` cannot share them; it would have to be rebuilt over `HubBroker::with`. `Host` here serves the hub with the protocol's own messages (`clax_surface::wire`) and counts each key it performed, which is what the tests read of a host.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":157},"content_hash":"3e8e183bc392d3b47268f4108a8825d73e0046df466d237bcb42f27cb0633c61"},"summary":"Drive the in-process runs with clax-testkit's FakeHost and MemoryHub in place of this file's scripted host","supersedes":"db9b99ab77d9d64b789813b618aa442b31381f02bdac0c95d59241a1322d7498","tags":["revisit:MemoryHub is built over HubBroker, or the daemon's end-to-end test needs the same host in process","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/outside.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.518758Z","id":"11df6bf4829d396ff7cecd2b1655b241d49b5c2e2c59a200cb1605276cfa7abf","body":{"detail":"`no_source_of_the_run_loop_names_the_fixtures_surface` reads `src` of clax-bot and the crates it depends on (clax-bot-sandbox, clax-core, clax-rt, clax-sample, clax-store, clax-surface), which its Bazel target is given as test data (crates/clax-bot/BUILD.bazel). clax-http, clax-server, clax-worker and the rest are above this crate: giving their sources to this test would rerun it on every change to them. The daemon's end-to-end test is where the scan of every crate belongs. Test files (`tests.rs`, a `tests` directory, what follows `#[cfg(test)]`) are skipped: crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs replays the fixture and names its surface.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1291},"end":{"line":1299},"content_hash":"286dd4e0ed8dbe3373c0a159df21e0779e828d1310ddc3c8a65004190811918c"},"summary":"The scan for the fixture's surface name reads the run loop's crates only, not the daemon's","supersedes":"58c11eaab393884959c2c2de7cfc06669946adda9ed6c7ea3e86a276de9bd6e8","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/policy.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.713686Z","id":"bed90b95530097e038895f73248f19411f2134685518be2735f9c68d3d320084","body":{"detail":"`seed_a_long_run` opens the test database beside the store's connection and inserts into `bot_steps (run_id, n, kind, started_at, committed_at, payload_json)` and updates `bot_runs.credits_milli`. A renamed or dropped column, or a new one that is `NOT NULL` with no default, fails the test loudly (the statements are unwrapped); a new column the run loop reads and a tick always sets would be absent on the seeded rows and read as its default, silently. The seeded turns are `pause_turn`s with no `assistant` blocks and an empty `usage`, which a tick does not write, and the run's credits have no usage rows behind them (the ledger and `credits_milli` disagree by 100,000 credits). The folds read them as a run of 5,000 committed steps whose transcript is the request alone, so the test holds that no count of steps, credits or days stops a run, and its own documentation says it does not see a bound on a history's size. The person is `claxbot_unenforced`, so `affordable` returns before the week's credits are read; `a_run_with_no_cap_on_credits_spends_past_the_settings_and_finishes` covers that path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":579},"end":{"line":617},"content_hash":"c65bd90191aee06d6bb5c665a229872df49743a858004c8c7f19e5582d9aa0a1"},"suggested_fix":"If the store gains a way to commit a step without a tick (as its own tests do with `begin_step` and `commit_step`), seed through it so a migration cannot pass this test by; until then the SQL is a fair price for a test that 5,000 ticks would make slow.","summary":"The run of 5,000 steps is written by SQL that names the store's columns, with turns no tick writes and no usage rows: what it holds, and what a schema change does to it","supersedes":"7475b1bda257f32b7d0b7ec92ee3ae5b7f0d19cde3b5d5c04d74afbb108f4e46","tags":["review","verify-t4","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.927943Z","id":"69e620b7cf77b22a3c9c1f3b3212b051940278bf3b00260f83784660c9ea9d02","body":{"detail":"Deleted in 0e3d282a6 feat(claxbot): Clax's own surface is a provider in src/clax, and the proof drives it. Left open for the owner to close.","kind":"comment","references":"51b21b23df995cfda3596f8c8207fa3ae1b8d0443e1f287a92eeba0de80ac724","summary":"The code this record is about was deleted and nothing took its place: The test adapter (struct ClaxProvider over BotHost in tests/seam.rs, with its own policy, draft_op and publish) was deleted; the proof now drives the crate's own provider (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs, through seam.rs fn provider), so there is no second copy of the glue to compare.","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.928546Z","id":"500162fa8d7f1be8658154acc4a5fbc9d634d7cf73ee5b7a9f4102ea8d9c402b","body":{"detail":"`Left` compares a step's journal rows (step, attempt, seq, op, ok, result), the fake host's writes by key and operation (a reply's thread also), the calls that reached it, the script's value, the step's `calls` without `ms`, five payload fields, `published` in the tool result, and the stored draft. Not compared: a journal row's `args_hash`; a write's arguments (a reply's body, a publish's note, addresses and files; the published version's files); the rest of the tool result and of the payload (`result`, `outcome`, `tool_use_id`); the events emitted; the audit records (`bot.script`, `bot.call` and its `replayed`); usage. `Stepper` (446-515) builds none of those and asserts on a diverged replay instead of answering it. No script here has a refused publish, a write the host's plan refuses, a publish without `addresses`, a cancelled script (`StepEnd::Cancelled` is never passed) or a declared web call. Each of these was made, one at a time, to `ClaxSession` and then to crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, and `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::` passed all three tests: a refused publish not journaled (seam.rs 339; script.rs 399-401); a host write refused by its plan not journaled (seam.rs 362; script.rs 422-424); the publish's `note` dropped (seam.rs 324; script.rs 327); the default `addresses` dropped (seam.rs 313; script.rs 315). Nine others failed on both sides, as they should: a draft operation journaled with its value, a policy refusal not journaled, a replayed host write or publish reaching the host, `published` missing from the tool result, a draft row dropped on the replayed attempt, a replayed publish not moving the draft, a replayed reply not counted, a replayed rebase going to the current version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":438},"content_hash":"e914a186df46dd85a538ab3c9619b4b2bf01040d08ace678ecaa567aba3759e6"},"suggested_fix":"Before script.rs moves: add a script whose publish is refused (`conflict`, someone published first) and whose host write is refused by the plan (`FakeState::fail_next`), one that publishes with no `addresses`, and a cancelled one; and compare the writes' arguments.","summary":"What the proof of the seam does not compare, and four changes, made to the adapter and to today's code alike, that it does not notice","supersedes":"fd5ba3b8dee5f8c47f2082d41a20acb430e0c0ffa12f742b7138d2589ad960c3","tags":["review","seam","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:29.209360Z","id":"2f29c9e8ff81c0f9c7c472905c2edd883ca9513d0251c3462e809b9f3a54c5a1","body":{"detail":"`RacedToThePage` writes, from inside the source's fetch, a journal row and a page of the same URL at place 500 of the open step (`Store::spend_journaled`, with the driver the test minted), so the fetch under way is refused `page_exists`. The store has no hook to fail one write or one read: a provider's conformance fixture, which is not given the driver, cannot make `clax` answer `Answer::unwritten` (crates/clax-bot/tests/providers.rs names the case not applicable), and the committed half of record 785c9e30 (a read of the run's row failing with the claim held) cannot be driven at all. A `fail_next` on the tests' store, as `FakeBotHost` has, would let both be played.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1802},"end":{"line":1807},"content_hash":"2fec9d3eac3005fdf2b0c5ba4c711ae2345338856fa203a5ce540910f4886c24"},"summary":"The one test of a web transaction the store refuses makes it fail by a page kept at another place of the same step, which takes the driver's ID","supersedes":"79e2c3250a4a689c28d2a26429aa1c858506a0685c641f3ea513f5b3962839ec","tags":["t5","fix-round","for-t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
